{
  "source_poem_zh": "更能消几番风雨，\n匆匆春又归去。\n惜春长怕花开早，\n何况落红无数。",
  "critical_units": [
    {
      "id": "song_04_u1",
      "source_span": "更能消几番风雨",
      "meaning": "反问还能承受几番风雨，语气中含春光易逝的忧虑。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_04_u2",
      "source_span": "匆匆春又归去",
      "meaning": "把春天写成匆忙离开的对象。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_04_u3",
      "source_span": "惜春长怕花开早",
      "meaning": "因爱惜春光而担心花期过早。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_04_u4",
      "source_span": "落红无数",
      "meaning": "众多落花加强春将尽的感受。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x38478d708c7016",
      "translation": "How many more bouts of wind and rain can spring endure?\nIn haste, spring too has gone away.\nCherishing spring, I have long feared it would bloom too soon—\nall the more so now, with fallen blossoms beyond count.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xd84ccf10bcc74d",
      "translation": "How many more storms can spring endure?—\nIn haste, it slips away again.\nI grieve for spring, forever fearing the blossoms open too soon;\nAnd now, how much more, with fallen petals without number.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x0b157e8d6ebbe2",
      "translation": "How many more rounds of wind and rain can it endure?\nIn haste, spring has gone away again.\nLoving spring, I’ve long feared the flowers would bloom too soon—\nAnd more so now, with countless fallen petals.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x0067b915766c21",
      "translation": "How many more bouts of wind and rain can spring endure?\nSo swiftly, spring is leaving once again.\nThose who cherish spring always fear the flowers bloom too soon—\nHow much harder to bear the countless fallen petals.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xe2f599ed3d1367",
      "translation": "How many more rounds of wind and rain can spring endure?\nIn haste, spring has gone away again.\nThose who grieve for spring have long feared its flowers would bloom too soon—\nall the more so now, with countless petals falling.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xe37a61586177a4",
      "translation": "How many more storms can it withstand?\nIn haste, spring once more departs.\nCherishing spring, I have long feared the flowers blooming too soon—\nall the more so when fallen petals lie scattered without end.",
      "notes": []
    }
  ]
}

