      "source_span": "竹杖芒鞋轻胜马",
      "meaning": "把徒步装备写得胜过骑马，轻重可含心境意味。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_08_u4",
      "source_span": "一蓑烟雨任平生",
      "meaning": "以蓑衣烟雨概括从容面对风雨，可兼指现实天气与人生处境。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x81e2805374ec79",
      "translation": "Pay no mind to rain that lashes through the trees;\nwhy not chant and whistle, walking on at ease?\nWith bamboo staff and straw sandals, I am lighter than a horse—\nwho could be afraid?\nIn mist and rain, one simple cloak\nis enough for all my life.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x4574a11bbe9f00",
      "translation": "Listen not to the rain beating through the trees and striking the leaves; why not sing aloud and stroll at ease?\nWith a bamboo staff and straw sandals, I’m lighter than on horseback. Who’s afraid? In a rain cape, I’ll meet mist and rain throughout my life.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x5738aed37701d9",
      "translation": "Hear not the rain beating through the trees and striking the leaves; why not hum and whistle as you stroll at ease?\nA bamboo staff and straw sandals feel lighter than a horse. Who’s afraid? In a cloak of mist and rain, I’ll face the years ahead.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x57721ffb404518",
      "translation": "Pay no heed to rain rattling through the trees; why not stroll on slowly, humming as you go?\nA bamboo staff and straw sandals feel lighter than a horse. Who’s afraid? Let me face the mist and rain, all my life long.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x8e17ea73e1c7fa",
      "translation": "Heed not the rain that beats through woods and leaves.\nWhy not sing out, and take your time to walk?\nBamboo staff, straw sandals—lighter than a horse.\nWho’s afraid?\nOne straw cape: let mist and rain\ncome as they will, my whole life long.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x93706dc22fe0f5",
      "translation": "Heed not the rain threading the woods and beating the leaves.\nWhy not chant and whistle, and walk at ease?\nWith bamboo staff and straw sandals, I go lighter than on horseback.\nWho’s afraid?\nIn a straw rain cape, let me face a lifetime of mist and rain.",
      "notes": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "source_poem_zh": "雨横风狂三月暮，\n门掩黄昏、无计留春住；\n泪眼问花花不语，\n乱红飞过秋千去。",
  "critical_units": [
    {
      "id": "song_09_u1",
      "source_span": "雨横风狂三月暮",
      "meaning": "以晚春风雨交加写季节将尽。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_09_u2",
      "source_span": "无计留春住",
      "meaning": "把春光当作可以挽留却无法留住的对象。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_09_u3",
      "source_span": "泪眼问花花不语",
      "meaning": "未明示身份的问者向花发问，花被写成沉默的回应者。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_09_u4",
      "source_span": "乱红飞过秋千去",
      "meaning": "飞散的落花带走春日景象，也没有给出明确回答。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "xa38ab6fe1e3c49",
      "translation": "Rain lashes, wild winds rage at spring’s end;\nAt dusk, the door is shut—no way to keep spring here.\nThrough tearful eyes I ask the flowers; they do not answer.\nScattered red petals fly past the swing.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xd838958389f83d",
      "translation": "Rain lashes sideways, wind runs wild as the third month wanes;\nThe door is closed on dusk—no way to make spring stay.\nThrough tear-filled eyes I ask the flowers; the flowers give no answer.\nA flurry of red petals flies beyond the swing.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x9a421fabf5f986",
      "translation": "Rain lashes, wind rages, at the close of spring;\nAt dusk the door is shut—no way to keep spring here.\nWith tearful eyes I ask the flowers; they do not speak,\nWhile scattered red petals fly past the swing and away.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xb345aaf58396a0",
      "translation": "Rain lashes sideways, wind runs wild—the third month wanes.\nThe door is shut against the dusk; no way to make spring stay.\nThrough tear-filled eyes I ask the flowers; the flowers give no answer.\nRed petals swirl and scatter, flying past the swing.",
      "notes": [
        "The third month of the traditional Chinese calendar falls in late spring."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xd3d458b766212f",
      "translation": "Rain lashes, wind rages, late in spring;\\nThe door is shut at dusk—no way to keep spring here.\\nThrough tearful eyes I ask the flowers; they do not speak,\\nWhile scattered petals fly past the swing and away.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x66320d4ee88d80",
      "translation": "Rain lashes sideways, wind runs wild;\nthe third month wanes.\nAt dusk I close the gate—\nno way to make spring stay.\nThrough tear-filled eyes I ask the flowers;\nthe flowers give no answer.\nRed petals, scattered in the wind,\nfly past the empty swing.",
      "notes": [
        "The third month is the final month of spring in the traditional Chinese calendar."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

