{
  "source_poem_zh": "红藕香残玉簟秋。\n轻解罗裳，独上兰舟。\n云中谁寄锦书来？雁字回时，月满西楼。\n花自飘零水自流，一种相思，两处闲愁。\n此情无计可消除，才下眉头，却上心头。",
  "critical_units": [
    {
      "id": "song_10_u1",
      "source_span": "轻解罗裳，独上兰舟",
      "meaning": "省略动作主体，呈现独自整理衣裳后登舟的行动。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_10_u2",
      "source_span": "云中谁寄锦书来",
      "meaning": "以问句期待远方来信，寄信者未指明。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_10_u3",
      "source_span": "一种相思，两处闲愁",
      "meaning": "同一相思分置两地，写双方可能共享的愁绪。"
    },
    {
      "id": "song_10_u4",
      "source_span": "才下眉头，却上心头",
      "meaning": "愁绪从眉间转到心头，以空间转换表现难以排遣。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x7d0c019f85741f",
      "translation": "The red lotus fades; its fragrance thins—\na jade mat chilled by autumn.\nI softly loosen my silken robe,\nand board the orchid boat alone.\nWho, through the clouds, will send a brocade letter?\nWhen the geese return in formation,\nthe moon will fill the western tower.\nFlowers drift of themselves, water flows on;\none longing, two places of quiet sorrow.\nThis feeling has no way to be erased:\njust leaving my brows,\nit rises again within my heart.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xc673b45a53b431",
      "translation": "The red lotus fades, its fragrance lingering on the jade mat in autumn.\nI loosen my silken robes and, alone, board the orchid boat.\nWho will send a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen the wild geese return in formation, the moon will fill the western tower.\nFlowers drift of themselves; water flows of itself—\none longing, two places steeped in quiet sorrow.\nThere is no way to banish this feeling:\nscarcely lowered from my brows, it rises again within my heart.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xa49e8758211d6e",
      "translation": "Red lotus fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade-smooth mat.\nGently I loosen my silk robe,\nalone I board the orchid boat.\nWho sends a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen wild geese return in written ranks,\nmoonlight fills the western chamber.\n\nFlowers drift down; water flows on.\nOne longing,\ntwo places of lonely sorrow.\nThere is no way to banish this feeling:\njust as it leaves my brow,\nit rises in my heart.",
      "notes": [
        "“Brocade letter” means a cherished letter; migrating geese traditionally evoke messages carried between separated lovers.",
        "The “jade-smooth mat” is a cool sleeping mat; “orchid boat” is a poetic name for an elegant boat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xcdcebb365b33cf",
      "translation": "Red lotus fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade-smooth mat.\nLightly I loosen my silk robes,\nand board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a silken letter through the clouds?\nWhen geese return in written ranks,\nmoonlight fills the western tower.\n\nFlowers drift away; water flows on.\nOne longing,\ntwo places of quiet sorrow.\nThere is no way to banish this feeling:\njust as it leaves my brow,\nit rises in my heart.",
      "notes": [
        "“Written ranks” preserves the image of geese flying in formations like written characters, with its suggestion of letters carried from afar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xa1fcf5df3b63ab",
      "translation": "The red lotus’s fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade mat.\nI slip off my silk robe and board the orchid boat alone.\nWho will send a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen the wild geese return in formation, the moon fills the western tower.\nFlowers drift of themselves; water flows of itself—\none longing, two places of quiet sorrow.\nThis feeling cannot be dispelled:\nscarcely lowered from my brows, it rises again within my heart.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x9c8fbfbfdf7629",
      "translation": "Red lotus fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade-smooth mat.\nGently loosening my silken robe, I board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen geese return in lettered ranks,\nmoonlight fills the western chamber.\nFlowers drift away, water flows on—\none longing,\ntwo places of quiet sorrow.\nThere is no way to banish this feeling:\njust as it leaves my brows,\nit rises in my heart.",
      "notes": [
        "“Orchid boat” is a poetic term for a fine boat; “brocade letter” means a precious, intimate letter.",
        "The geese’s formation resembles written characters. Geese also traditionally evoke letters carried across great distances."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "source_poem_zh": "玉阶生白露，\n夜久侵罗袜。\n却下水精帘，\n玲珑望秋月。",
  "critical_units": [
    {
      "id": "tang_03_u1",
      "source_span": "夜久侵罗袜",
      "meaning": "夜深露重，露意写到罗袜被沾湿的程度。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tang_03_u2",
      "source_span": "却下水精帘",
      "meaning": "动作主体省略，可理解为退入帘内并放下帘幕。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tang_03_u3",
      "source_span": "玲珑望秋月",
      "meaning": "隔着晶亮帘幕望秋月；“玲珑”的具体修饰对象留有余地。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "xf43d80c417e15a",
      "translation": "White dew gathers on the jade steps;\nDeep into the night, it soaks her silk stockings.\nShe lowers the crystal curtain,\nAnd gazes through its shimmering weave at the autumn moon.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xdebc5e1590a3b8",
