  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "xfc8a3a2f0de452",
      "translation": "How much more wind and rain can spring endure?\nIn haste, once more, spring slips away.\nI treasure spring, and fear the flowers bloom too soon—\nHow much harder, then, to see red petals fallen beyond counting.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xd0a15c3dc82c15",
      "translation": "How many more storms can spring withstand?\nIn haste, it turns and goes.\nThose who love spring always fear the flowers bloom too soon—\nWhat of the countless fallen blooms?",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x71502abb46bcb1",
      "translation": "How many more bouts of wind and rain can spring endure?\nIn such haste, spring departs once more.\nCherishing spring, I always fear the flowers bloom too soon—\nHow much more, then, when fallen petals lie beyond counting.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xe9d44428ae37e0",
      "translation": "How many more storms\ncan spring withstand?\nIn haste, spring leaves again.\nThose who grieve for spring\nhave long feared the flowers bloom too soon—\nhow much more, with petals falling everywhere.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xfcd47ea589112d",
      "translation": "How many more rounds of wind and rain can it endure?\nIn haste, spring has gone away again.\nI cherish spring, and always fear the flowers will bloom too soon—\nall the more so now, with countless blossoms fallen.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x3c2b3de2553cb7",
      "translation": "How many more storms can we endure?\nIn haste, spring has gone again.\nI cherish spring, yet dread the flowers blooming too soon—\nAnd now, how many fallen petals lie scattered.",
