      "translation": "Heed not the rain piercing the woods and beating the leaves;\nWhy not chant and whistle, and walk at ease?\nBamboo staff and straw sandals—lighter than riding a horse.\nWho fears?\nA straw cape, mist and rain—let them be mine for all my days.",
