      "translation": "Heed not the rain that lashes leaves and threads the woods;\nWhy not chant and whistle, walking at ease?\nBamboo staff and straw sandals—lighter than riding a horse.\nWho’s afraid?\nA straw cloak, a lifetime of mist and rain—let them come.",
      "notes": []
