      "translation": "Listen not to the rain beating through the trees,\nwhy not sing aloud and stroll at ease?\nBamboo staff, straw sandals—lighter than a horse.\nWho’s afraid? In a rain cape through mist and rain,\nI’ll spend my life this way.",
