    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xb966e6123756c3",
      "translation": "Pay no heed to rain piercing the woods and beating the leaves;\nWhy not chant and whistle, and walk at ease?\nWith bamboo staff and straw sandals, I travel lighter than on horseback.\nWho’s afraid?\nIn a straw rain cape, let me weather mist and rain all my life.",
